  "id": "COMPOUND:29473 - PROTEIN:5826",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but consistent relationship between (Z)-7-Hydroxynuciferol and SMMC-7721, mediated through a series of targets. The drug (Z)-7-Hydroxynuciferol is identified as a target for multiple compounds, including MOVP-3 and VMRC-LCP, which in turn target 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One. This compound is ultimately shown to have a target of SMMC-7721, a cell line that is likely involved in liver-related processes. The evidence is supported by a shared pathway involving 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, which links the drug to SMMC-7721 through a series of molecular interactions. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which (Z)-7-Hydroxynuciferol may influence SMMC-7721, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
